// Planet 0: Injectia (web code review)
QB.push(
{"id": "H25-1.1-w1", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "single", "q": ["Eksamen 2025, oppgave 1.1 (Node.js + PostgreSQL, campus-markedsplass). Hvilken linje i innloggingsruten har den alvorligste sårbarheten som kan nås <b>uten</b> å være innlogget?", "Exam 2025, task 1.1 (Node.js + PostgreSQL campus marketplace). Which line in the login route holds the most severe vulnerability reachable <b>without</b> being logged in?"], "c": "22 | // login route\n23 | app.post('/login', async (req, res) => {\n24 |   const { email, password } = req.body;\n25 |   // intentionally simplified \"hash\"\n26 |   const user = await db.query(\n27 |     `SELECT id, email FROM users WHERE email = '${email}' AND password = md5('${password}') LIMIT 1;`\n28 |   );\n29 |   if (user.rows.length) {\n30 |     const payload = { id: user.rows[0].id, email: user.rows[0].email, role: 'user' };\n31 |     const b64 = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(payload)).toString('base64');\n32 |     res.cookie('session', b64, { signed: true, httpOnly: false, sameSite: 'lax' });\n33 |     return res.redirect('/dashboard');\n34 |   }\n35 |   return res.status(401).send('Invalid credentials');\n36 | });", "o": [["Linje 27: SQL-injeksjon, <code>email</code> og <code>password</code> settes rett inn i SQL-strengen", "Line 27: SQL injection, <code>email</code> and <code>password</code> are pasted straight into the SQL string"], ["Linje 33: åpen omdirigering via <code>res.redirect</code>", "Line 33: open redirect via <code>res.redirect</code>"], ["Linje 24: mass assignment fordi hele <code>req.body</code> brukes", "Line 24: mass assignment because the whole <code>req.body</code> is used"], ["Linje 35: brukeropplisting fordi feilmeldingen avslører om e-posten finnes", "Line 35: user enumeration because the error reveals whether the email exists"]], "a": 0, "w": ["Linje 27 bygger SQL med template-literal: brukerens <code>email</code>/<code>password</code> blir en del av <b>koden</b>, ikke data. En angriper kan avslutte strengen med <code>'</code> og endre WHERE-logikken → innlogging som en vilkårlig bruker uten passord (autentiseringsomgåelse, kontoovertakelse). Dette er det første funnet man skal skrive: uautentisert og høy alvorlighet. Fiks: parameterisert spørring (<code>$1</code>, <code>$2</code>).", "Line 27 builds SQL with a template literal: the user's <code>email</code>/<code>password</code> become part of the <b>code</b>, not data. An attacker can close the string with <code>'</code> and change the WHERE logic → log in as an arbitrary user without the password (authentication bypass, account takeover). This is the finding to write first: unauthenticated and high severity. Fix: a parameterised query (<code>$1</code>, <code>$2</code>)."], "x": [null, ["Målet er fast (<code>'/dashboard'</code>), ikke brukerstyrt, så det er ingen åpen omdirigering.", "The target is fixed (<code>'/dashboard'</code>), not user-controlled, so there is no open redirect."], ["Bare <code>email</code> og <code>password</code> plukkes ut og ingen objekt-felter skrives til databasen fra body. Ikke mass assignment.", "Only <code>email</code> and <code>password</code> are destructured, and no object fields from the body are written to the DB. Not mass assignment."], ["Samme melding (<code>Invalid credentials</code>) uansett om e-post eller passord er feil, så den avslører ikke noe.", "The same message (<code>Invalid credentials</code>) is returned whether the email or password is wrong, so it reveals nothing."]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w2", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilken påvirkning (CIA) har SQL-injeksjonen på linje 27 i verste fall?", "What is the worst-case impact (CIA) of the SQL injection on line 27?"], "c": "26 |   const user = await db.query(\n27 |     `SELECT id, email FROM users WHERE email = '${email}' AND password = md5('${password}') LIMIT 1;`\n28 |   );", "o": [["Bare tilgjengelighet: serveren kan krasje", "Availability only: the server may crash"], ["Bare at angriperen får vite om en e-post er registrert", "Only that the attacker learns whether an email is registered"], ["Konfidensialitet og integritet: logge inn som hvilken som helst bruker og lese/endre dataene deres", "Confidentiality and integrity: log in as any user and read/change their data"], ["Kjøring av skallkommandoer på serveren", "Execution of shell commands on the server"]], "a": 2, "w": ["Angriperen kontrollerer WHERE-betingelsen og får en gyldig, signert sesjonscookie for en annen brukers <code>id</code> → kontoovertakelse. Det rammer <b>C</b> (lese andres annonser og data) og <b>I</b> (opprette/slette i offerets navn). I svaret: navn + linje, hva som går galt, C/I/A-påvirkning, PoC, fiks.", "The attacker controls the WHERE condition and receives a valid, signed session cookie for another user's <code>id</code> → account takeover. That hits <b>C</b> (read others' listings and data) and <b>I</b> (create/delete in the victim's name). In the answer: name + line, what goes wrong, C/I/A impact, PoC, fix."], "x": [["En feilformet spørring kan gi feil, men verst er kontoovertakelse, ikke krasj.", "A malformed query may error, but the worst case is account takeover, not a crash."], ["Det er mye mer enn opplisting: hele WHERE-logikken kan endres.", "It is much more than enumeration: the whole WHERE logic can be changed."], null, ["Koden kaller ikke <code>exec</code>/<code>system</code>, så skallkommandoer er ikke den direkte følgen. (Stablede spørringer kan i tillegg gi DROP/DELETE, og med en superbruker-DB i verste fall <code>COPY … FROM PROGRAM</code>, men kontoovertakelse via C og I er det klare hovedsvaret.)", "The code does not call <code>exec</code>/<code>system</code>, so shell commands are not the direct consequence. (Stacked queries could also allow DROP/DELETE, and with a superuser DB role even <code>COPY … FROM PROGRAM</code>, but account takeover via C and I is the clear main answer.)"]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w3", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "tf", "q": ["Sant eller usant: Hvis angriperen bruker SQL-injeksjonen på linje 27 til å logge inn som administratorens e-post, får de også tilgang til <code>/admin/promote</code>.", "True or false: if the attacker uses the SQL injection on line 27 to log in as the administrator's email, they also get access to <code>/admin/promote</code>."], "c": "29 |   if (user.rows.length) {\n30 |     const payload = { id: user.rows[0].id, email: user.rows[0].email, role: 'user' };\n31 |     const b64 = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(payload)).toString('base64');\n32 |     res.cookie('session', b64, { signed: true, httpOnly: false, sameSite: 'lax' });\n33 |     return res.redirect('/dashboard');\n   ...\n75 | // admin: promote user\n76 | app.post('/admin/promote', async (req, res) => {\n77 |   const me = currentUser(req);\n78 |   if (!me || me.role !== 'admin') return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');\n79 |   const { email } = req.body;", "o": [["Sant", "True"], ["Usant", "False"]], "a": 1, "w": ["<b>Usant.</b> Linje 30 hardkoder <code>role: 'user'</code> i cookien uansett hvem som logger inn, og <code>/admin/promote</code> (linje 78) sjekker <code>me.role</code> fra cookien, ikke fra databasen. Admin-rollen kan bare oppnås ved å forfalske cookien, som krever signeringshemmeligheten (se den svake hemmeligheten på linje 9). Les koden nøye før du påstår en kjede.", "<b>False.</b> Line 30 hard-codes <code>role: 'user'</code> in the cookie whoever logs in, and <code>/admin/promote</code> (line 78) checks <code>me.role</code> from the cookie, not from the database. The admin role can only be obtained by forging the cookie, which needs the signing secret (see the weak secret on line 9). Read the code carefully before claiming a chain."], "x": [["Rollen kommer fra linje 30 (alltid <code>'user'</code>), ikke fra databaseraden.", "The role comes from line 30 (always <code>'user'</code>), not from the database row."], null]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w4", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilken fiks lukker sårbarheten på linje 27 korrekt? (<code>db</code> eksporterer <code>query(text, params)</code>.)", "Which fix correctly closes the vulnerability on line 27? (<code>db</code> exports <code>query(text, params)</code>.)"], "c": "26 |   const user = await db.query(\n27 |     `SELECT id, email FROM users WHERE email = '${email}' AND password = md5('${password}') LIMIT 1;`\n28 |   );", "o": [["Kjøre <code>xss(email)</code> og <code>xss(password)</code> før spørringen", "Run <code>xss(email)</code> and <code>xss(password)</code> before the query"], ["Validere e-postformatet med JavaScript i nettleseren", "Validate the email format with JavaScript in the browser"], ["Bytte <code>md5</code> ut med <code>sha256</code> i spørringen", "Replace <code>md5</code> with <code>sha256</code> in the query"], ["<code>db.query('… WHERE email = $1 …', [email, …])</code> med plassholdere, og hente hashen for sjekk med bcrypt/Argon2", "<code>db.query('… WHERE email = $1 …', [email, …])</code> with placeholders, and fetch the hash to check with bcrypt/Argon2"]], "a": 3, "w": ["Parameteriserte spørringer sender SQL-teksten og verdiene <b>separat</b> til PostgreSQL, så input kan aldri bli SQL-kode. Bonus: lagre passord med salt + treg hash (bcrypt/Argon2id) og sammenlign i appen, ikke unsaltet <code>md5</code> i SQL.", "Parameterised queries send the SQL text and the values <b>separately</b> to PostgreSQL, so input can never become SQL code. Bonus: store passwords with salt + a slow hash (bcrypt/Argon2id) and compare in the app, not unsalted <code>md5</code> in SQL."], "x": [["<code>xss</code> filtrerer HTML for utdata, ikke SQL-spesialtegn som <code>'</code>. Feil verktøy, feil kontekst.", "<code>xss</code> filters HTML for output, not SQL metacharacters like <code>'</code>. Wrong tool, wrong context."], ["Klientvalidering omgås trivielt (curl/Burp sender rett til serveren).", "Client-side validation is trivially bypassed (curl/Burp send straight to the server)."], ["Endrer bare hashfunksjonen; strengen settes fortsatt inn i SQL, så injeksjonen består.", "Only changes the hash function; the string is still pasted into SQL, so the injection remains."], null]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w5", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hva er den grunnleggende svakheten i sesjonshåndteringen (linje 9, 12–20, 30–32)?", "What is the fundamental weakness in the session handling (lines 9, 12–20, 30–32)?"], "c": " 8 | app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));\n 9 | app.use(cookieParser('supersecret')); // cookie signature only\n10 | \n11 | // naive session handling\n12 | function currentUser(req) {\n13 |   try {\n14 |     const raw = req.signedCookies.session;\n15 |     if (!raw) return null;\n16 |     return JSON.parse(Buffer.from(raw, 'base64').toString('utf8'));\n17 |   } catch {\n18 |     return null;\n19 |   }\n20 | }\n   ...\n30 |     const payload = { id: user.rows[0].id, email: user.rows[0].email, role: 'user' };\n31 |     const b64 = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(payload)).toString('base64');\n32 |     res.cookie('session', b64, { signed: true, httpOnly: false, sameSite: 'lax' });", "o": [["Cookien er ikke signert, så hvem som helst kan endre den", "The cookie is not signed, so anyone can edit it"], ["Identitet og rolle lagres hos klienten og beskyttes bare av en hardkodet, gjettbar hemmelighet (<code>'supersecret'</code>)", "Identity and role are stored client-side, protected only by a hard-coded, guessable secret (<code>'supersecret'</code>)"], ["<code>JSON.parse</code> kjører kode, så dette er usikker deserialisering med RCE", "<code>JSON.parse</code> runs code, so this is insecure deserialisation with RCE"], ["Base64 er for svak kryptering; den bør byttes til AES", "Base64 is too weak an encryption; it should be replaced by AES"]], "a": 1, "w": ["<code>signed: true</code> + <code>req.signedCookies</code> sjekker en HMAC, så endring uten nøkkel avvises. Men nøkkelen <code>'supersecret'</code> står i kildekoden og er lett å gjette. Den som kjenner den kan signere en egen <code>{id, role}</code> → utgi seg for hvem som helst, også <code>admin</code> (brudd på C, I). I tillegg stoler serveren på rollen i cookien i stedet for å slå den opp i databasen.", "<code>signed: true</code> + <code>req.signedCookies</code> check an HMAC, so edits without the key are rejected. But the key <code>'supersecret'</code> is in the source and easy to guess. Whoever knows it can sign their own <code>{id, role}</code> → impersonate anyone, including <code>admin</code> (breaks C, I). Also the server trusts the role in the cookie instead of looking it up in the database."], "x": [["Feil: <code>signed: true</code> og <code>signedCookies</code> verifiserer en HMAC-signatur.", "Wrong: <code>signed: true</code> and <code>signedCookies</code> verify an HMAC signature."], null, ["<code>JSON.parse</code> lager bare data (objekter, strenger, tall); den kjører ikke kode. Ikke påstå funn som ikke finnes.", "<code>JSON.parse</code> only builds data (objects, strings, numbers); it runs no code. Don't claim issues that aren't there."], ["Base64 er koding, ikke kryptering, men problemet er autentisitet (hvem som kan lage cookien), ikke konfidensialitet.", "Base64 is encoding, not encryption, but the problem is authenticity (who can create the cookie), not confidentiality."]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w6", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilken fiks er best for sesjonssvakheten?", "Which fix is best for the session weakness?"], "c": " 8 | app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));\n 9 | app.use(cookieParser('supersecret')); // cookie signature only\n10 | \n11 | // naive session handling\n12 | function currentUser(req) {\n13 |   try {\n14 |     const raw = req.signedCookies.session;\n15 |     if (!raw) return null;\n16 |     return JSON.parse(Buffer.from(raw, 'base64').toString('utf8'));\n17 |   } catch {\n18 |     return null;\n19 |   }\n20 | }\n   ...\n30 |     const payload = { id: user.rows[0].id, email: user.rows[0].email, role: 'user' };\n31 |     const b64 = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(payload)).toString('base64');\n32 |     res.cookie('session', b64, { signed: true, httpOnly: false, sameSite: 'lax' });", "o": [["Bytte base64 ut med heksadesimal koding av JSON-en", "Replace base64 with hexadecimal encoding of the JSON"], ["Sette <code>sameSite: 'none'</code> slik at cookien alltid sendes", "Set <code>sameSite: 'none'</code> so that the cookie is always sent"], ["Lang tilfeldig hemmelighet fra miljøvariabel, helst serverlagrede sesjoner der rollen slås opp i DB, og <code>httpOnly: true</code>", "A long random secret from an environment variable, ideally server-side sessions where the role is looked up in the DB, and <code>httpOnly: true</code>"], ["Gi cookien et mindre forutsigbart navn enn <code>session</code>", "Give the cookie a less predictable name than <code>session</code>"]], "a": 2, "w": ["Rot-årsak: forfalskbar klientstate. Fiks: sterk, hemmelig, roterbar nøkkel (ikke i kildekoden), eller en tilfeldig sesjons-ID der identitet og rolle ligger på serveren/databasen. Sjekk rollen mot DB ved hver admin-handling. <code>httpOnly: true</code> hindrer at XSS leser cookien.", "Root cause: forgeable client-side state. Fix: a strong, secret, rotatable key (not in the source), or a random session ID with identity and role kept on the server/DB. Check the role against the DB on every admin action. <code>httpOnly: true</code> stops XSS from reading the cookie."], "x": [["Bare en annen koding; den kan fortsatt signeres med den kjente nøkkelen.", "Just another encoding; it can still be signed with the known key."], ["Svekker CSRF-vernet og løser ikke forfalskning.", "Weakens CSRF protection and does not stop forgery."], null, ["Sikkerhet gjennom tilsløring; navnet står uansett i kildekoden.", "Security through obscurity; the name is in the source anyway."]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w7", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "multi", "q": ["Velg alle utsagn om cookie-innstillingene på linje 32 som er sanne.", "Select all true statements about the cookie options on line 32."], "c": "30 |     const payload = { id: user.rows[0].id, email: user.rows[0].email, role: 'user' };\n31 |     const b64 = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(payload)).toString('base64');\n32 |     res.cookie('session', b64, { signed: true, httpOnly: false, sameSite: 'lax' });", "o": [["<code>httpOnly: false</code> lar injisert JavaScript lese cookien via <code>document.cookie</code>", "<code>httpOnly: false</code> lets injected JavaScript read the cookie via <code>document.cookie</code>"], ["<code>sameSite: 'lax'</code> gjør at nettleseren ikke sender cookien med POST-skjemaer fra andre nettsteder", "<code>sameSite: 'lax'</code> means the browser does not send the cookie with POST forms from other sites"], ["<code>signed: true</code> krypterer innholdet slik at brukeren ikke kan lese id og rolle", "<code>signed: true</code> encrypts the content so the user cannot read id and role"], ["Endrer man <code>role</code> i base64-teksten uten ny signatur, godtas cookien", "Changing <code>role</code> in the base64 text without re-signing makes the cookie accepted"], ["Fordi rollen ligger i cookien, kan serveren ikke trekke tilbake en rolle før cookien byttes", "Because the role lives in the cookie, the server cannot revoke a role until the cookie changes"]], "a": [0, 1, 4], "w": ["httpOnly skjuler cookien for JS; her er den av, så en XSS kan stjele sesjonen. SameSite=Lax sender cookien ved toppnivå-GET-navigasjon, men ikke ved kryss-site POST, som demper CSRF mot POST-rutene. Signering gir integritet, ikke konfidensialitet. Klientlagret rolle kan ikke trekkes tilbake fra serveren.", "HttpOnly hides the cookie from JS; here it is off, so an XSS can steal the session. SameSite=Lax sends the cookie on top-level GET navigation but not on cross-site POST, which mitigates CSRF on the POST routes. Signing gives integrity, not confidentiality. A client-stored role cannot be revoked from the server."], "x": [["Sant: det er nettopp det httpOnly skal hindre.", "True: that is exactly what httpOnly is meant to prevent."], ["Sant: Lax sender bare cookien ved sikre toppnivå-navigasjoner (GET).", "True: Lax only sends the cookie on safe top-level navigations (GET)."], ["Usant: signering legger til en HMAC; innholdet er bare base64 og kan leses av alle.", "False: signing adds an HMAC; the content is just base64 and anyone can read it."], ["Usant: HMAC-sjekken feiler, <code>signedCookies.session</code> blir <code>false</code> og <code>currentUser</code> returnerer <code>null</code>.", "False: the HMAC check fails, <code>signedCookies.session</code> becomes <code>false</code> and <code>currentUser</code> returns <code>null</code>."], ["Sant: ingen serverstate, så en utstedt rolle gjelder til cookien endres.", "True: there is no server state, so an issued role holds until the cookie changes."]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w8", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilken sårbarhet finnes i <code>/listings/mine</code> (linje 54–64)?", "Which vulnerability is in <code>/listings/mine</code> (lines 54–64)?"], "c": "49 | // list mine\n50 | app.get('/listings/mine', async (req, res) => {\n51 |   const me = currentUser(req);\n52 |   if (!me) return res.status(401).send('Login required');\n53 |   const result = await db.query(`SELECT id, title, description, price FROM listings WHERE user_id=${me.id}`);\n54 |   const html = result.rows.map(\n55 |     r => `<div class=\"card\">\n56 |             <h3>${r.title}</h3>\n57 |             <p>${r.description}</p>\n58 |             <strong>${r.price}</strong>\n59 |             /listings/${r.id}/delete\n60 |               <button>Delete</button>\n61 |             </form>\n62 |           </div>`\n63 |   ).join('');\n64 |   res.send(`<html><body>${html}</body></html>`);\n65 | });", "o": [["Server-side template injection, fordi template-literals evaluerer <code>{{ }}</code>", "Server-side template injection, because template literals evaluate <code>{{ }}</code>"], ["Reflektert XSS fra en query-parameter", "Reflected XSS from a query parameter"], ["Lagret (stored) XSS: <code>title</code> og <code>description</code> fra databasen settes inn i HTML uten koding", "Stored XSS: <code>title</code> and <code>description</code> from the database are put into HTML without encoding"], ["Path traversal via <code>r.id</code> i lenken", "Path traversal via <code>r.id</code> in the link"]], "a": 2, "w": ["Verdiene ble lagret via <code>/listings/new</code> og skrives senere rått inn i HTML (linje 56–57). Et <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>-innhold i tittelen kjøres i nettleseren til den som ser siden. Sammen med <code>httpOnly: false</code> kan skriptet lese sesjonscookien. <code>xss</code>-biblioteket er importert (linje 5), men aldri brukt.", "The values were stored via <code>/listings/new</code> and later written raw into HTML (lines 56–57). <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> content in the title runs in the browser of whoever views the page. Combined with <code>httpOnly: false</code>, the script can read the session cookie. The <code>xss</code> library is imported (line 5) but never used."], "x": [["JS template-literals bruker <code>${}</code> på kodenivå og evaluerer aldri brukerdata; ingen template-motor, så ingen SSTI.", "JS template literals use <code>${}</code> at code level and never evaluate user data; there is no template engine, so no SSTI."], ["Ruten leser ingen query-parametere; dataene kommer fra databasen (lagret).", "The route reads no query parameters; the data comes from the database (stored)."], null, ["<code>r.id</code> er en SERIAL-heltall fra DB, og ingen fil åpnes.", "<code>r.id</code> is a SERIAL integer from the DB, and no file is opened."]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w9", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilken fiks lukker XSS-en i <code>/listings/mine</code>?", "Which fix closes the XSS in <code>/listings/mine</code>?"], "c": "54 |   const html = result.rows.map(\n55 |     r => `<div class=\"card\">\n56 |             <h3>${r.title}</h3>\n57 |             <p>${r.description}</p>\n58 |             <strong>${r.price}</strong>", "o": [["Bruke parameteriserte spørringer i <code>/listings/new</code>", "Use parameterised queries in <code>/listings/new</code>"], ["HTML-kode utdata (<code>&amp;</code> <code>&lt;</code> <code>&gt;</code> <code>\"</code> <code>'</code>), f.eks. med det importerte <code>xss</code>, pluss CSP og <code>httpOnly: true</code>", "HTML-encode the output (<code>&amp;</code> <code>&lt;</code> <code>&gt;</code> <code>\"</code> <code>'</code>), e.g. with the imported <code>xss</code>, plus CSP and <code>httpOnly: true</code>"], ["Sette <code>sameSite: 'strict'</code> på sesjonscookien", "Set <code>sameSite: 'strict'</code> on the session cookie"], ["Begrense tittelen til 50 tegn", "Limit the title to 50 characters"]], "a": 1, "w": ["XSS fikses der data møter HTML: <b>output-koding</b> etter kontekst. CSP (<code>script-src 'self'</code>) er forsvar i dybden, og <code>httpOnly</code> hindrer cookietyveri.", "XSS is fixed where data meets HTML: <b>context-aware output encoding</b>. CSP (<code>script-src 'self'</code>) is defence in depth, and <code>httpOnly</code> prevents cookie theft."], "x": [["Stopper SQLi, men <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> lagres da som vanlig data og skrives fortsatt rått ut.", "Stops SQLi, but <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> is then stored as ordinary data and still written out raw."], null, ["SameSite handler om CSRF, ikke om skript i siden.", "SameSite is about CSRF, not script in the page."], ["En kort payload som <code>&lt;svg onload=…&gt;</code> får plass; lengdegrense er ikke koding.", "A short payload like <code>&lt;svg onload=…&gt;</code> fits; a length limit is not encoding."]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w10", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "multi", "q": ["Hvilke linjer bygger SQL ved å lime inn verdier fra request-body eller URL (dvs. SQL-injeksjon)?", "Which lines build SQL by pasting in values from the request body or URL (i.e. SQL injection)?"], "c": "42 |   const { title, description, price } = req.body;\n43 |   await db.query(\n44 |     `INSERT INTO listings (user_id, title, description, price) VALUES (${me.id}, '${title}', '${description}', ${price});`\n45 |   );\n   ...\n53 |   const result = await db.query(`SELECT id, title, description, price FROM listings WHERE user_id=${me.id}`);\n   ...\n71 |   await db.query(`DELETE FROM listings WHERE id=${req.params.id} AND user_id=${me.id}`);\n   ...\n78 |   if (!me || me.role !== 'admin') return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');\n79 |   const { email } = req.body;\n80 |   await db.query(`UPDATE users SET role='moderator' WHERE email='${email}'`);", "o": [["Linje 44 (<code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>price</code>)", "Line 44 (<code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>price</code>)"], ["Linje 71 (<code>req.params.id</code>)", "Line 71 (<code>req.params.id</code>)"], ["Linje 80 (<code>email</code>), men bare nåbar for en admin", "Line 80 (<code>email</code>), but only reachable by an admin"], ["Linje 53, fordi <code>me.id</code> kommer rett fra request-body", "Line 53, because <code>me.id</code> comes straight from the request body"], ["Ingen: <code>db.query</code> escaper automatisk", "None: <code>db.query</code> escapes automatically"]], "a": [0, 1, 2], "w": ["44: tre body-felt (og <code>price</code> uten anførselstegn). 71: URL-segmentet <code>:id</code> limes inn uten anførselstegn. 80: <code>email</code> limes inn, men bak rollesjekken på linje 78 (lavere alvorlighet alene, høy i kjede med forfalsket cookie). 53 bruker <code>me.id</code> fra den signerte cookien, ikke fra body. <code>db.query(text, params)</code> er trygg bare når <code>params</code> faktisk brukes.", "44: three body fields (and <code>price</code> unquoted). 71: the URL segment <code>:id</code> is pasted in unquoted. 80: <code>email</code> is pasted in, but behind the role check on line 78 (lower severity alone, high when chained with a forged cookie). 53 uses <code>me.id</code> from the signed cookie, not from the body. <code>db.query(text, params)</code> is safe only when <code>params</code> is actually used."], "x": [["Sant: body-verdier interpoleres i INSERT.", "True: body values are interpolated into the INSERT."], ["Sant: rute-parameteren interpoleres i DELETE.", "True: the route parameter is interpolated into the DELETE."], ["Sant: interpolert, men bak <code>me.role !== 'admin'</code>.", "True: interpolated, but behind <code>me.role !== 'admin'</code>."], ["Usant: <code>me</code> kommer fra den signerte cookien via <code>currentUser</code>.", "False: <code>me</code> comes from the signed cookie via <code>currentUser</code>."], ["Usant: uten <code>params</code> sendes strengen som den er.", "False: without <code>params</code> the string is sent as-is."]]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w11", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "tf", "q": ["Sant eller usant: Linje 71 er en IDOR: en innlogget bruker kan slette en annen brukers annonse bare ved å sette dens <code>id</code> i URL-en.", "True or false: line 71 is an IDOR: a logged-in user can delete another user's listing just by putting its <code>id</code> in the URL."], "c": "67 | // delete listing\n68 | app.post('/listings/:id/delete', async (req, res) => {\n69 |   const me = currentUser(req);\n70 |   if (!me) return res.status(401).send('Login required');\n71 |   await db.query(`DELETE FROM listings WHERE id=${req.params.id} AND user_id=${me.id}`);\n72 |   res.redirect('/listings/mine');\n73 | });", "o": [["Sant", "True"], ["Usant", "False"]], "a": 1, "w": ["<b>Usant.</b> <code>AND user_id=${me.id}</code> er en eierskapssjekk, så en vanlig annen <code>id</code> sletter ingenting. Den ekte feilen er <b>SQL-injeksjon</b> via <code>req.params.id</code>: input som endrer WHERE-logikken kan omgå eierskapssjekken (integritet og tilgjengelighet: andres annonser slettes). Fiks: <code>db.query('DELETE … WHERE id=$1 AND user_id=$2', [id, me.id])</code>. Ikke påstå IDOR når sjekken finnes.", "<b>False.</b> <code>AND user_id=${me.id}</code> is an ownership check, so a plain other <code>id</code> deletes nothing. The real bug is <b>SQL injection</b> via <code>req.params.id</code>: input that changes the WHERE logic can bypass the ownership check (integrity and availability: others' listings deleted). Fix: <code>db.query('DELETE … WHERE id=$1 AND user_id=$2', [id, me.id])</code>. Don't claim IDOR when the check is there."], "x": [["Eierskapssjekken <code>user_id=${me.id}</code> stopper en ren id-bytte.", "The ownership check <code>user_id=${me.id}</code> stops a plain id swap."], null]},
{"id": "H25-1.1-w12", "t": 0, "s": "e25", "kind": "multi", "q": ["Velg alle <b>reelle</b> svakheter i tillegg til injeksjonene.", "Select all <b>real</b> weaknesses besides the injections."], "c": " 1 | // app.js\n 2 | const express = require('express');\n 3 | const cookieParser = require('cookie-parser');\n 4 | const db = require('./db'); // exports query(text, params)\n 5 | const xss = require('xss'); // currently unused\n 6 | const app = express();\n 7 | \n 8 | app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));\n 9 | app.use(cookieParser('supersecret')); // cookie signature only\n   ...\n25 |   // intentionally simplified \"hash\"\n26 |   const user = await db.query(\n27 |     `SELECT id, email FROM users WHERE email = '${email}' AND password = md5('${password}') LIMIT 1;`", "o": [["Passord lagres som usaltet MD5 (raskt å knekke)", "Passwords are stored as unsalted MD5 (fast to crack)"], ["<code>xss</code>-biblioteket er importert men aldri brukt på utdata", "The <code>xss</code> library is imported but never used on output"], ["Ingen rate-begrensning på <code>/login</code> (passordgjetting)", "No rate limiting on <code>/login</code> (password guessing)"], ["<code>express.urlencoded</code> gir XXE", "<code>express.urlencoded</code> gives XXE"], ["<code>app.listen(3000)</code> uten TLS er hovedfunnet", "<code>app.listen(3000)</code> without TLS is the main finding"]], "a": [0, 1, 2], "w": ["MD5 uten salt: lekkede hasher knekkes med oppslagstabeller/GPU; bruk Argon2id/bcrypt. Ubrukt <code>xss</code>: utdata kodes ikke. Ingen rate limit: brute force mot innlogging. XXE krever en XML-parser, og oppgaven sier at HTTPS termineres i reverse proxy.", "Unsalted MD5: leaked hashes fall to lookup tables/GPUs; use Argon2id/bcrypt. Unused <code>xss</code>: output is not encoded. No rate limit: brute force against login. XXE needs an XML parser, and the task says HTTPS terminates at the reverse proxy."], "x": [["Sant: se skjemaet (<code>stored as md5(password)</code>).", "True: see the schema (<code>stored as md5(password)</code>)."], ["Sant: kommentaren på linje 5 sier det selv.", "True: the comment on line 5 says so."], ["Sant: ingenting begrenser antall forsøk.", "True: nothing limits the number of attempts."], ["Usant: URL-kodede skjemaer er ikke XML.", "False: URL-encoded forms are not XML."], ["Usant: oppgaven sier «assume HTTPS at the reverse proxy».", "False: the task says “assume HTTPS at the reverse proxy”."]]},
{"id": "H23-6-w1", "t": 0, "s": "e23", "kind": "single", "q": ["Eksamen 2023 «Spot the vuln»: Hvilken sårbarhetsklasse er dette, og hva er verste innvirkning?", "Exam 2023 “Spot the vuln”: which vulnerability class is this, and what is the worst impact?"], "c": "# Whitelisted URL\nwhitelist_pattern = re.compile(r'^https?://safe.ntnu.no/.*$')\n\n@app.route('/fetch_resource', methods=['GET'])\ndef fetch_resource():\n    # Get the URL parameter from the request\n    url = request.args.get('url')\n\n    if not url:\n        return jsonify({'error': 'Missing URL parameter'}), 400\n\n    # Check if the provided URL is whitelisted\n    if not whitelist_pattern.match(url):\n        return jsonify({'error': 'URL is not whitelisted'}), 403\n\n    try:\n        # Make an HTTP GET request to the specified URL\n        response = requests.get(url)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception for HTTP errors\n\n        # Return the content of the response\n        return jsonify({'content': response.text})\n\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        return jsonify({'error': f'Request to {url} failed: {str(e)}'}), 500\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)", "o": [["Åpen omdirigering: brukeren sendes til en ondsinnet side", "Open redirect: the user is sent to a malicious site"], ["SSRF: serveren henter en URL brukeren styrer, og kan nå interne tjenester og sky-metadata (f.eks. <code>169.254.169.254</code>)", "SSRF: the server fetches a URL the user controls and can reach internal services and cloud metadata (e.g. <code>169.254.169.254</code>)"], ["Reflektert XSS via <code>response.text</code>", "Reflected XSS via <code>response.text</code>"], ["Path traversal via <code>url</code>", "Path traversal via <code>url</code>"]], "a": 1, "w": ["(1) Feilen: <code>requests.get(url)</code> med brukerstyrt URL, beskyttet av en svak allow-list-regex. (2) Utnyttelse: få regexen til å godta en URL som ender på en annen vert enn tiltenkt (punktumene er ikke escapet), eller via omdirigeringer. (3) Innvirkning: serveren blir en proxy inn i det interne nettet → lese interne tjenester/admin-paneler, sky-metadata med nøkler (C), portskanning via feilmeldingene.", "(1) The bug: <code>requests.get(url)</code> with a user-controlled URL, guarded by a weak allow-list regex. (2) Exploitation: get the regex to accept a URL that ends up at a different host than intended (the dots are not escaped), or via redirects. (3) Impact: the server becomes a proxy into the internal network → read internal services/admin panels, cloud metadata with keys (C), port scanning via the error messages."], "x": [["Brukeren omdirigeres ikke; det er <b>serveren</b> som gjør forespørselen.", "The user is not redirected; the <b>server</b> makes the request."], null, ["<code>jsonify</code> svarer med <code>application/json</code>, så innholdet tolkes ikke som HTML.", "<code>jsonify</code> answers with <code>application/json</code>, so the content is not rendered as HTML."], ["Ingen fil åpnes lokalt; URL-en hentes over HTTP.", "No local file is opened; the URL is fetched over HTTP."]]},
{"id": "H23-6-w2", "t": 0, "s": "e23", "kind": "multi", "q": ["Velg alle svakheter i koden som er reelle.", "Select all weaknesses in the code that are real."], "c": "# Whitelisted URL\nwhitelist_pattern = re.compile(r'^https?://safe.ntnu.no/.*$')\n\n@app.route('/fetch_resource', methods=['GET'])\ndef fetch_resource():\n    # Get the URL parameter from the request\n    url = request.args.get('url')\n\n    if not url:\n        return jsonify({'error': 'Missing URL parameter'}), 400\n\n    # Check if the provided URL is whitelisted\n    if not whitelist_pattern.match(url):\n        return jsonify({'error': 'URL is not whitelisted'}), 403\n\n    try:\n        # Make an HTTP GET request to the specified URL\n        response = requests.get(url)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception for HTTP errors\n\n        # Return the content of the response\n        return jsonify({'content': response.text})\n\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        return jsonify({'error': f'Request to {url} failed: {str(e)}'}), 500\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)", "o": [["Punktumene i regexen er ikke escapet, så <code>.</code> matcher hvilket som helst tegn (f.eks. vertsnavnet <code>safe-ntnu.no</code>)", "The dots in the regex are not escaped, so <code>.</code> matches any character (e.g. the host name <code>safe-ntnu.no</code>)"], ["<code>requests.get</code> følger omdirigeringer, så en tillatt vert som omdirigerer kan sende serveren til en intern adresse", "<code>requests.get</code> follows redirects, so an allowed host that redirects can send the server to an internal address"], ["<code>debug=True</code> eksponerer Werkzeug-debuggeren og stakkspor", "<code>debug=True</code> exposes the Werkzeug debugger and stack traces"], ["<code>re.match</code> uten <code>^</code> godtar URL-er som bare inneholder <code>safe.ntnu.no</code> et sted", "<code>re.match</code> without <code>^</code> accepts URLs that only contain <code>safe.ntnu.no</code> somewhere"], ["Feilmeldingen gjentar <code>str(e)</code>, så angriperen ser forskjellen på «connection refused» og timeout (portskanning)", "The error message echoes <code>str(e)</code>, so the attacker sees the difference between “connection refused” and timeout (port scanning)"]], "a": [0, 1, 2, 4], "w": ["Regexen er forankret (<code>^</code> … <code>$</code>, og <code>match</code> starter i posisjon 0), men <code>.</code> er et jokertegn, så andre vertsnavn matcher. Omdirigeringer sjekkes ikke mot allow-listen. Debug-modus og ordrette feilmeldinger lekker informasjon. Sjekket i Python: <code>https://safe-ntnu.no/x</code> matcher, <code>https://safe.ntnu.no.evil.com/</code> og <code>https://safe.ntnu.no@evil.com/</code> gjør det ikke.", "The regex is anchored (<code>^</code> … <code>$</code>, and <code>match</code> starts at position 0), but <code>.</code> is a wildcard, so other host names match. Redirects are not checked against the allow-list. Debug mode and verbatim error messages leak information. Checked in Python: <code>https://safe-ntnu.no/x</code> matches, <code>https://safe.ntnu.no.evil.com/</code> and <code>https://safe.ntnu.no@evil.com/</code> do not."], "x": [["Sant: <code>safe.ntnu.no</code> bør være <code>safe\\.ntnu\\.no</code>.", "True: <code>safe.ntnu.no</code> should be <code>safe\\.ntnu\\.no</code>."], ["Sant: <code>allow_redirects=True</code> er standard for GET.", "True: <code>allow_redirects=True</code> is the default for GET."], ["Sant: aldri debug i produksjon.", "True: never debug in production."], ["Usant: mønsteret har <code>^</code>, og <code>re.match</code> forankrer uansett i starten.", "False: the pattern has <code>^</code>, and <code>re.match</code> anchors at the start anyway."], ["Sant: ulike feil avslører hvilke interne porter som er åpne.", "True: different errors reveal which internal ports are open."]]},
{"id": "H23-6-w3", "t": 0, "s": "e23", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilken fiks er best for <code>/fetch_resource</code>?", "Which fix is best for <code>/fetch_resource</code>?"], "c": "# Whitelisted URL\nwhitelist_pattern = re.compile(r'^https?://safe.ntnu.no/.*$')\n\n@app.route('/fetch_resource', methods=['GET'])\ndef fetch_resource():\n    # Get the URL parameter from the request\n    url = request.args.get('url')\n\n    if not url:\n        return jsonify({'error': 'Missing URL parameter'}), 400\n\n    # Check if the provided URL is whitelisted\n    if not whitelist_pattern.match(url):\n        return jsonify({'error': 'URL is not whitelisted'}), 403\n\n    try:\n        # Make an HTTP GET request to the specified URL\n        response = requests.get(url)\n        response.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception for HTTP errors\n\n        # Return the content of the response\n        return jsonify({'content': response.text})\n\n    except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:\n        return jsonify({'error': f'Request to {url} failed: {str(e)}'}), 500\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True)", "o": [["Legge til <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code> på svaret", "Add <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code> to the response"], ["Svarteliste strengene <code>localhost</code> og <code>127.0.0.1</code>", "Blacklist the strings <code>localhost</code> and <code>127.0.0.1</code>"], ["HTML-kode <code>response.text</code> før den returneres", "HTML-encode <code>response.text</code> before returning it"], ["Parse URL-en, sammenlign <code>hostname</code> eksakt mot en allow-list, slå av omdirigeringer, avvis interne IP-er etter DNS-oppslag, og slå av debug", "Parse the URL, compare <code>hostname</code> exactly against an allow-list, disable redirects, reject internal IPs after DNS resolution, and turn debug off"]], "a": 3, "w": ["SSRF fikses med en streng <b>allow-list</b> på parsed vertsnavn (ikke regex på hele strengen), <code>allow_redirects=False</code> (eller valider hvert hopp), blokkering av private/link-local-adresser etter oppslag (mot DNS-rebinding), nettverkssegmentering/egress-filter, og generiske feilmeldinger.", "SSRF is fixed with a strict <b>allow-list</b> on the parsed host name (not a regex over the whole string), <code>allow_redirects=False</code> (or validate every hop), blocking private/link-local addresses after resolution (against DNS rebinding), network segmentation/egress filtering, and generic error messages."], "x": [["Klikkjakking-header; påvirker ikke hva serveren henter.", "A clickjacking header; does not affect what the server fetches."], ["Svartelister omgås (<code>0.0.0.0</code>, <code>[::1]</code>, <code>2130706433</code>, egne DNS-navn).", "Blacklists are bypassed (<code>0.0.0.0</code>, <code>[::1]</code>, <code>2130706433</code>, own DNS names)."], ["Svaret er JSON, og problemet er hvilke verter serveren når, ikke XSS.", "The response is JSON, and the problem is which hosts the server reaches, not XSS."], null]},
{"id": "H24-2-w1", "t": 0, "s": "e24", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hva er hovedgrunnen til en SQL-injeksjonssårbarhet?", "What is the main reason for an SQL injection vulnerability?"], "o": [["Buffer overflows i webserverprogramvare", "Buffer overflows in web server software"], ["Cross-site scripting", "Cross-site scripting"], ["Svak inputvalidering i webapplikasjoner", "Weak input validation in web applications"], ["Uoppdaterte operativsystemer", "Unpatched operating systems"]], "a": 2, "w": ["Eksamenssvaret er «svak inputvalidering». Mer presist: brukerinput blandes inn i SQL-teksten (<code>'…' + input</code>), så data tolkes som kode. Den riktige fiksen er <b>parameteriserte spørringer</b> (<code>?</code>, <code>$1</code>); validering og allow-lists er forsvar i dybden.", "The exam answer is “weak input validation”. More precisely: user input is mixed into the SQL text (<code>'…' + input</code>), so data is interpreted as code. The correct fix is <b>parameterised queries</b> (<code>?</code>, <code>$1</code>); validation and allow-lists are defence in depth."], "x": [["Minnefeil i webserveren er en helt annen klasse (binær utnyttelse).", "Memory bugs in the web server are a different class entirely (binary exploitation)."], ["XSS er en annen injeksjon (i HTML/JS i nettleseren), ikke årsaken til SQLi.", "XSS is a different injection (into HTML/JS in the browser), not the cause of SQLi."], null, ["SQLi ligger i applikasjonskoden og finnes også på fullt oppdaterte systemer.", "SQLi lives in the application code and exists on fully patched systems too."]]},
{"id": "n0-01", "t": 0, "s": "new", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilken sårbarhet er dette, og hva er riktig fiks?", "Which vulnerability is this, and what is the correct fix?"], "c": "app.get('/download', (req, res) => {\n  const file = req.query.file;\n  res.sendFile(path.join(__dirname, 'uploads', file));\n});", "o": [["Path traversal/LFI; løs stien med <code>path.resolve</code> og avvis alt som ikke ligger under <code>uploads/</code> (eller slå opp filen via en ID)", "Path traversal/LFI; resolve the path with <code>path.resolve</code> and reject anything outside <code>uploads/</code> (or look the file up by an ID)"], ["Path traversal; fjern alle forekomster av <code>../</code> én gang med <code>replace</code>", "Path traversal; remove every <code>../</code> once with <code>replace</code>"], ["SSRF; bruk en allow-list av verter", "SSRF; use an allow-list of hosts"], ["IDOR; legg til CSRF-token", "IDOR; add a CSRF token"]], "a": 0, "w": ["<code>path.join</code> normaliserer <code>../</code>, så <code>file=../../../../etc/passwd</code> peker ut av <code>uploads/</code> → lese vilkårlige filer (C: kildekode, nøkler, <code>.env</code>). Fiks: <code>const p = path.resolve(base, file); if (!p.startsWith(base + path.sep)) return 403;</code>, eller bare la brukeren velge en ID fra en tabell (allow-list).", "<code>path.join</code> normalises <code>../</code>, so <code>file=../../../../etc/passwd</code> points out of <code>uploads/</code> → read arbitrary files (C: source, keys, <code>.env</code>). Fix: <code>const p = path.resolve(base, file); if (!p.startsWith(base + path.sep)) return 403;</code>, or only let the user pick an ID from a table (allow-list)."], "x": [null, ["Ett pass med <code>replace</code> omgås med <code>....//</code> (blir <code>../</code> etter fjerning) eller URL-koding.", "A single <code>replace</code> pass is bypassed with <code>....//</code> (becomes <code>../</code> after removal) or URL encoding."], ["Ingen nettverksforespørsel gjøres; det er en lokal fil.", "No network request is made; it is a local file."], ["Problemet er filstien, ikke objekt-eierskap eller CSRF.", "The problem is the file path, not object ownership or CSRF."]]},
{"id": "n0-02", "t": 0, "s": "new", "kind": "single", "q": ["En pentester sender denne forespørselen. Hvilken sårbarhet tester den, og hva er fiksen?", "A pentester sends this request. Which vulnerability does it test, and what is the fix?"], "c": "POST /api/import HTTP/1.1\nContent-Type: application/xml\n\n<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE r [ <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\"> ]>\n<item><name>&x;</name></item>", "o": [["XSS; HTML-kode <code>name</code> ved utskrift", "XSS; HTML-encode <code>name</code> on output"], ["XXE; slå av DTD-er/eksterne entiteter i XML-parseren", "XXE; disable DTDs/external entities in the XML parser"], ["Path traversal; fjern <code>../</code> fra filnavn", "Path traversal; strip <code>../</code> from file names"], ["Usikker deserialisering; signer XML-en", "Insecure deserialisation; sign the XML"]], "a": 1, "w": ["<code>&lt;!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///…\"&gt;</code> definerer en <b>ekstern entitet</b>. Hvis parseren løser den, erstattes <code>&amp;x;</code> med filinnholdet → fillesing (C), og med <code>http://</code>-URL-er også SSRF. Fiks: slå av DTD-behandling/eksterne entiteter (f.eks. <code>defusedxml</code> i Python, <code>disallow-doctype-decl</code> i Java), eller bruk JSON.", "<code>&lt;!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///…\"&gt;</code> defines an <b>external entity</b>. If the parser resolves it, <code>&amp;x;</code> is replaced by the file content → file read (C), and with <code>http://</code> URLs also SSRF. Fix: disable DTD processing/external entities (e.g. <code>defusedxml</code> in Python, <code>disallow-doctype-decl</code> in Java), or use JSON."], "x": [["Ingen HTML/skript i payloaden; angrepet skjer i XML-parseren på serveren.", "No HTML/script in the payload; the attack happens in the XML parser on the server."], null, ["Filstien står i en entitet, ikke i en filnavn-parameter; fjerning av <code>../</code> hjelper ikke mot <code>file:///etc/passwd</code>.", "The path is in an entity, not a file name parameter; stripping <code>../</code> does not help against <code>file:///etc/passwd</code>."], ["Signering stopper ikke parseren fra å løse entiteter i signerte dokumenter.", "Signing does not stop the parser from resolving entities in signed documents."]]},
{"id": "n0-03", "t": 0, "s": "new", "kind": "multi", "q": ["Velg alle utdragene som er <b>sårbare</b>. (Ikke påstå funn som ikke finnes.)", "Select all snippets that are <b>vulnerable</b>. (Don't claim issues that aren't there.)"], "c": "A: db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [req.params.id])\nB: exec('ping -c 1 ' + req.query.host)\nC: const user = jwt.decode(req.headers.token)   // used to authorise\nD: data = pickle.loads(base64.b64decode(request.cookies['prefs']))\nE: execFile('ping', ['-c', '1', req.query.host])\nF: cursor.execute(\"SELECT * FROM items WHERE name = ?\", (name,))", "o": [["A", "A"], ["B", "B"], ["C", "C"], ["D", "D"], ["E", "E"], ["F", "F"]], "a": [1, 2, 3], "w": ["B: kommandoinjeksjon, <code>exec</code> går via skallet. C: <code>jwt.decode</code> verifiserer <b>ikke</b> signaturen → forfalskede tokens godtas; bruk <code>jwt.verify</code> med fast algoritme (avvis <code>alg: none</code>). D: <code>pickle.loads</code> på klientdata = usikker deserialisering → RCE. A, F: parameteriserte spørringer (<code>$1</code>, <code>?</code>) er trygge. E: <code>execFile</code> med argumentliste starter ikke et skall, så ingen kommandoinjeksjon.", "B: command injection, <code>exec</code> goes through the shell. C: <code>jwt.decode</code> does <b>not</b> verify the signature → forged tokens accepted; use <code>jwt.verify</code> with a fixed algorithm (reject <code>alg: none</code>). D: <code>pickle.loads</code> on client data = insecure deserialisation → RCE. A, F: parameterised queries (<code>$1</code>, <code>?</code>) are safe. E: <code>execFile</code> with an argument list starts no shell, so no command injection."], "x": [["Trygg: <code>$1</code>-plassholder, verdien sendes separat.", "Safe: <code>$1</code> placeholder, the value is sent separately."], ["Sårbar: skallet tolker <code>;</code>, <code>||</code>, <code>&#36;( )</code> i <code>host</code>.", "Vulnerable: the shell interprets <code>;</code>, <code>||</code>, <code>&#36;( )</code> in <code>host</code>."], ["Sårbar: decode leser bare innholdet uten å sjekke signaturen.", "Vulnerable: decode only reads the content without checking the signature."], ["Sårbar: pickle kan kjøre vilkårlig kode under lasting.", "Vulnerable: pickle can run arbitrary code while loading."], ["Trygg mot kommandoinjeksjon: argumentene går rett til programmet.", "Safe from command injection: the arguments go straight to the program."], ["Trygg: <code>?</code>-plassholder.", "Safe: <code>?</code> placeholder."]]},
{"id": "n0-04", "t": 0, "s": "new", "kind": "single", "q": ["Hvilke to feil har denne ruten?", "Which two bugs does this route have?"], "c": "app.put('/api/users/:id', requireLogin, async (req, res) => {\n  await User.update(req.params.id, req.body);   // body: { name, email, ... }\n  res.json({ ok: true });\n});\n// users table: id, name, email, password_hash, role", "o": [["SQL-injeksjon og XSS", "SQL injection and XSS"], ["CSRF og manglende HSTS", "CSRF and missing HSTS"], ["IDOR (ingen sjekk av at <code>:id</code> er din egen) og mass assignment (hele <code>req.body</code>, også <code>role</code>, skrives)", "IDOR (no check that <code>:id</code> is your own) and mass assignment (the whole <code>req.body</code>, including <code>role</code>, is written)"], ["Path traversal og SSRF", "Path traversal and SSRF"]], "a": 2, "w": ["<code>requireLogin</code> sjekker bare autentisering, ikke <b>autorisasjon</b>: hvem som helst kan endre en annen bruker (IDOR → I, kontoovertakelse ved å bytte e-post). <code>req.body</code> sendes rett til modellen, så et ekstra felt som <code>role</code> blir lagret (mass assignment → rettighetseskalering). Fiks: <code>if (req.params.id != req.user.id &amp;&amp; !isAdmin) 403</code>, og en allow-list: <code>const { name, email } = req.body</code>.", "<code>requireLogin</code> only checks authentication, not <b>authorisation</b>: anyone can modify another user (IDOR → I, account takeover by changing the email). <code>req.body</code> goes straight to the model, so an extra field like <code>role</code> gets stored (mass assignment → privilege escalation). Fix: <code>if (req.params.id != req.user.id &amp;&amp; !isAdmin) 403</code>, and an allow-list: <code>const { name, email } = req.body</code>."], "x": [["Ingen rå SQL eller HTML-utdata vises; ORM-kallet er ikke det problematiske.", "No raw SQL or HTML output is shown; the ORM call is not the problem."], ["PUT med JSON er ikke det sentrale, og HSTS handler om transport.", "PUT with JSON is not the central issue, and HSTS is about transport."], null, ["Ingen filsti eller utgående URL.", "No file path or outbound URL."]]},
{"id": "n0-05", "t": 0, "s": "new", "kind": "tf", "q": ["Sant eller usant: Hvis <code>email</code> inneholder <code>' OR 1=1 --</code>, returnerer spørringen alle aktive brukere.", "True or false: if <code>email</code> contains <code>' OR 1=1 --</code>, the query returns all active users."], "c": "const r = await db.query(\n  'SELECT id FROM users WHERE email = $1 AND active = true', [email]);", "o": [["Sant", "True"], ["Usant", "False"]], "a": 1, "w": ["<b>Usant.</b> Med plassholderen <code>$1</code> sendes SQL-teksten og verdien separat (prepared/extended protocol). Hele strengen <code>' OR 1=1 --</code> sammenlignes som én e-postverdi og matcher ingen. I en kodegjennomgang skal dette <b>ikke</b> rapporteres som SQLi; det gir trekk å påstå feil som ikke finnes.", "<b>False.</b> With the placeholder <code>$1</code>, the SQL text and the value are sent separately (prepared/extended protocol). The whole string <code>' OR 1=1 --</code> is compared as a single email value and matches nothing. In a code review this must <b>not</b> be reported as SQLi; claiming non-existent bugs costs points."], "x": [["Verdien blir aldri en del av SQL-koden.", "The value never becomes part of the SQL code."], null]},
{"id": "n0-06", "t": 0, "s": "new", "kind": "multi", "q": ["Payload-matching (kompendiets jukselapp): velg alle <b>riktige</b> par payload → sårbarhet.", "Payload matching (kompendium cheat sheet): select all <b>correct</b> payload → vulnerability pairs."], "o": [["<code>$(whoami)</code> → kommandoinjeksjon", "<code>$(whoami)</code> → command injection"], ["<code>&lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt;</code> → XSS", "<code>&lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt;</code> → XSS"], ["<code>http://169.254.169.254/</code> → SSRF", "<code>http://169.254.169.254/</code> → SSRF"], ["<code>../../../etc/passwd</code> → SQL-injeksjon", "<code>../../../etc/passwd</code> → SQL injection"], ["<code>{{7*'7'}}</code> → format string", "<code>{{7*'7'}}</code> → format string"], ["<code>&lt;!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\"&gt;</code> → XXE", "<code>&lt;!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\"&gt;</code> → XXE"]], "a": [0, 1, 2, 5], "w": ["Jukselappen: <code>' OR 1=1 --</code>, <code>admin'--</code>, <code>' or sleep(10); --</code> → SQLi; <code>; id</code>, <code>|| id</code>, <code>$(whoami)</code> → kommandoinjeksjon; <code>{{7*7}}</code>, <code>{{7*'7'}}</code> → SSTI; <code>\"&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt;</code> → XSS; <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080</code>, <code>http://169.254.169.254/</code> → SSRF; <code>../../../etc/passwd</code> → path traversal/LFI; <code>%p %x %n</code> → format string; <code>&lt;!ENTITY … SYSTEM …&gt;</code> → XXE.", "Cheat sheet: <code>' OR 1=1 --</code>, <code>admin'--</code>, <code>' or sleep(10); --</code> → SQLi; <code>; id</code>, <code>|| id</code>, <code>$(whoami)</code> → command injection; <code>{{7*7}}</code>, <code>{{7*'7'}}</code> → SSTI; <code>\"&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt;</code> → XSS; <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080</code>, <code>http://169.254.169.254/</code> → SSRF; <code>../../../etc/passwd</code> → path traversal/LFI; <code>%p %x %n</code> → format string; <code>&lt;!ENTITY … SYSTEM …&gt;</code> → XXE."], "x": [["Riktig: kommandosubstitusjon i skallet.", "Correct: command substitution in the shell."], ["Riktig: <code>onerror</code> kjører JS når bildet ikke lastes.", "Correct: <code>onerror</code> runs JS when the image fails to load."], ["Riktig: sky-metadata-adressen, klassisk SSRF-mål.", "Correct: the cloud metadata address, a classic SSRF target."], ["Feil: <code>../</code> er path traversal/LFI.", "Wrong: <code>../</code> is path traversal/LFI."], ["Feil: <code>{{ }}</code> er template-syntaks → SSTI; format string er <code>%p</code>/<code>%x</code>/<code>%n</code>.", "Wrong: <code>{{ }}</code> is template syntax → SSTI; format string is <code>%p</code>/<code>%x</code>/<code>%n</code>."], ["Riktig: ekstern entitet i DTD → XXE.", "Correct: an external entity in a DTD → XXE."]]},
{"id": "n0-07", "t": 0, "s": "new", "kind": "single", "q": ["Du sender <code>{{7*'7'}}</code> i et navnefelt, og siden viser <code>7777777</code>. Hva har du sannsynligvis funnet?", "You send <code>{{7*'7'}}</code> in a name field and the page shows <code>7777777</code>. What have you most likely found?"], "o": [["XSS, fordi input vises på siden", "XSS, because input is shown on the page"], ["SQL-injeksjon i et <code>LIKE</code>-uttrykk", "SQL injection in a <code>LIKE</code> expression"], ["SSTI i en Python/Jinja2-lignende template-motor (streng × tall = repetisjon)", "SSTI in a Python/Jinja2-like template engine (string × number = repetition)"], ["Ingen sårbarhet; serveren gjentar bare input", "No vulnerability; the server just echoes input"]], "a": 2, "w": ["Templaten <b>evaluerte</b> uttrykket: i Python er <code>7*'7'</code> = <code>'7777777'</code> (Jinja2), mens Twig (PHP) gir <code>49</code>. Begge betyr SSTI, som ofte fører til RCE. Fiks: aldri bygg template-kildekode fra brukerinput; send input som <b>data</b> (<code>render_template('x.html', name=name)</code>), bruk sandkasse.", "The template <b>evaluated</b> the expression: in Python <code>7*'7'</code> = <code>'7777777'</code> (Jinja2), while Twig (PHP) gives <code>49</code>. Both mean SSTI, which often leads to RCE. Fix: never build template source from user input; pass input as <b>data</b> (<code>render_template('x.html', name=name)</code>), use a sandbox."], "x": [["Ren ekko ville vist <code>{{7*'7'}}</code> uendret; her ble det beregnet.", "A plain echo would show <code>{{7*'7'}}</code> unchanged; here it was computed."], ["SQL gir ikke strengrepetisjon av <code>{{ }}</code>-syntaks.", "SQL does not give string repetition from <code>{{ }}</code> syntax."], null, ["Uttrykket ble evaluert på serveren, så det er mer enn ekko.", "The expression was evaluated on the server, so it is more than an echo."]]}
);
